{
 "_what": "COOK TWO [the curb on the map] (10/18): the map's street with the curb's lip, face and shadow, from his tiles, one piece per road block, for RUN to lay in place of the flat band (__THE_STREETS_JOIN__).",
 "mask_bits": {
  "1": "east (x+1)",
  "2": "west (x-1)",
  "4": "south (y+1)",
  "8": "north (y-1)",
  "_how": "RUN's own loop in mapStreetTile: d = 0..3 -> mask |= 1 << d for every road neighbour"
 },
 "lay": "atlas = COOK2_MAP_CURB_<FAMILY>_<TW>.png, 16 pieces in a row (mask 0..15), each TW wide and TW/2 + face tall, two rows (the two variants; take row (x * 7 + y * 13) % 2 so a street never shows one piece twice running on a diagonal). For a road block: p = iso(x, y, ox, oy) (the block's top vertex); draw piece `mask` at (p.sx - TW/2, p.sy - face * TW/TWk) at width TW and height (TWk/2 + face) * TW/TWk, smoothing off, in the tile loop where the block's own art is drawn: BLOCK in place of the arterial picture (it is the whole road block), BAND where the band is drawn now (__THE_STREETS_JOIN__). TWk = the largest level at or under the block's device width (TW * CV_DPR), else the smallest: a piece is only ever enlarged (under 2x), never shrunk past its 1 px lip. Streets only (RUN's J value 1); the freeway keeps its band (a freeway has a shoulder, not a curb). A block on a deck or a dip keeps the band.",
